d response/write delays\"}}, \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\", \"source_ids\": [\"src_unstable_view_contract\", \"src_storage_completion_contract\", \"src_async_delivery\"], \"pending\": [], \"assessment\": \"unassessed\", \"candidate\": true, \"grounding\": {\"source_ids\": [\"src_step\", \"src_unstable_stable\", \"src_log_term_view\", \"src_log_slice_view\"], \"expectation_ids\": [\"src_unstable_view_contract\", \"src_storage_completion_contract\"], \"binding_ids\": [\"BIND_STORAGE_VIEW\"], \"derivation\": \"The unstable type contract requires retaining the in-progress logical view until writes are stabilized and guaranteed reflected by Storage queries. The storage-completion commentary explicitly requires waiting when in-progress appends can overwrite that view. Therefore, with a current accepted replacement pending and a different stored version, consuming an earlier completion must preserve the accepted entry returned by the logical log. This requirement concerns observable history consistency, not the particular implementation guard or unstable offset value.\", \"applicability\": \"Applicable to public RawNode asynchronous storage use with serialized calls, actual append producers, correctly ordered storage work and responses after write completion. Device durability is modeled by caller MemoryStorage without crash; the property does not claim crash recovery.\", \"unresolved\": [], \"conflicts\": [], \"alternatives\": [\"A different implementation could copy or reconstruct the accepted entry instead of retaining unstable memory; the oracle tests returned entry contents, not the storage strategy.\"]}, \"version\": 1}\nbindings {\"associations\": [{\"claim_id\": \"C_ACCEPTED_LOG_VIEW\", \"source_ids\": [\"src_unstable_view_contract\", \"src_storage_completion_contract\", \"src_step\", \"src_log_term_view\", \"src_log_slice_view\"], \"rationale\": \"Binds the required preserved view to the real completion consumer and overlay-backed read path.\"}], \"anchor\": {\"source_ids\": [\"src_step\"], \"boundary_complete\": false, \"kind\": \"declaration\", \"material_id\": \"src_step\", \"start_line\": 1085, \"end_line\": 1085, \"symbol\": \"raft.Step\"}, \"material_id\": \"src_step\", \"id\": \"BIND_STORAGE_VIEW\", \"file\": \"raft.go\", \"symbol\": \"raft.Step\", \"start_line\": 1158, \"end_line\": 1195, \"snapshot_id\": \"9d121cb0a05741bca550182e282b3479\", \"content_digest\": \"4283c10e12c6da14964c6d6784a69851af1312245aa83925ec0e9426a07ed7bb\", \"basis\": \"agent_inference\", \"description\": \"Dispatch of stale and current append completions determines whether unstable state is retired. Logical lookup consumers are separately cited for the observation boundary.\", \"pending\": [], \"excerpt\": \"\\t\\t} else if m.Type == pb.MsgStorageAppendResp {\\n\\t\\t\\tif m.Index != 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// Don't consider the appended log entries to be stable because\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// they may have been overwritten in the unstable log during a\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// later term. See the comment in newStorageAppendResp for more\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// about this race.\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Infof(\\\"%x [term: %d] ignored entry appends from a %s message with lower term [term: %d]\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tr.id, r.Term, m.Type, m.Term)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif m.Snapshot != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// Even if the snapshot applied under a different term, its\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// application is still valid. Snapshots carry committed\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t// (term-independent) state.\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.appliedSnap(m.Snapshot)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t// ignore other cases\\n\\t\\t\\tr.logger.Infof(\\\"%x [term: %d] ignored a %s message with lower term from %x [term: %d]\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tr.id, r.Term, m.Type, m.From, m.Term)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn nil\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tswitch m.Type {\\n\\tcase pb.MsgHup:\\n\\t\\tif r.preVote {\\n\\t\\t\\tr.hup(campaignPreElection)\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tr.hup(campaignElection)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\tcase pb.MsgStorageAppendResp:\\n\\t\\tif m.Index != 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\tr.raftLog.stableTo(entryID{term: m.LogTerm, index: m.Index})\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif m.Snapshot != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tr.appliedSnap(m.Snapshot)\\n\\t\\t}\", \"version\": 1}\nchecks {\"direct_check_id\": \"637e0d79cf4444ad8d1a66c0f2bcf0d8\", \"id\": \"ce685a3cf2234bbca54f8b07081bf7f0\", \"action\": \"direct_check\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"outcome\": \"tests_passed\", \"origin\": \"executed\", \"command\": [\"/usr/bin/bwrap\", \"--die-with-parent\", \"--new-session\", \"--unshare-net\", \"--ro-bind\", \"/\", \"/\", \"--tmpfs\", \"/home\", \"--tmpfs\", \"/root\", \"--tmpfs\", \"/tmp\", \"--dev\", \"/dev\", \"--proc\", \"/proc\", \"--bind\", \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run/experiments/b5c4048b0ee944d8911e8d96d7d6a0de/workspace\", \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run/experiments/b5c4048b0ee944d8911e8d96d7d6a0de/workspace\", \"--ro-bind\", \"/home/nitro/go/pkg/mod\", \"/home/nitro/go/pkg/mod\", \"--ro-bind\", \"/home/nitro/go/pkg/mod/golang.org/toolchain@v0.0.1-go1.26.7.linux-amd64\", \"/home/nitro/go/pkg/mod/golang.org/toolchain@v0.0.1-go1.26.7.linux-amd64\", \"--chdir\", \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run/experiments/b5c4048b0ee944d8911e8d96d7d6a0de/workspace\", \"--\", \"/home/nitro/go/pkg/mod/golang.org/toolchain@v0.0.1-go1.26.7.linux-amd64/bin/go\", \"test\", \"-json\", \"-count=1\", \"-timeout=600.0s\", \"-run\", \"^TestAssurance\", \".\"], \"cwd\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run/experiments/b5c4048b0ee944d8911e8d96d7d6a0de/workspace\", \"started_at\": \"2026-10-02T08:48:41.981046+00:00\", \"ended_at\": \"2026-10-02T08:48:54.437788+00:00\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"stdout\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run/logs/ce685a3cf2234bbca54f